  "result": "Perfect! I've found the discrepancy. The `search_index` table in the schema only spreads `tenantColumns` (which is just `org_id`), not `timestampColumns`. This means it has NO `updated_at` column—only `indexed_at`.\n\nHowever, the documentation in `tables-webhooks-search-and-infra.md` lists an index that doesn't exist:\n\n**In the documentation (line 186):**\n```\n| `search_index_org_updated_idx` | `org_id, updated_at` | no | letting the reindex job find the stalest documents first without a full scan\n```\n\n**In the actual schema (webhooks.ts lines 54-70):**\n- Only one index exists: `search_index_org_kind_idx` on `(org_id, subject_kind)`\n- The table has NO `updated_at` column; it has `indexed_at` instead\n\nThe documentation describes an index `search_index_org_updated_idx` over columns `(org_id, updated_at)` that the schema does not declare.\n\nANSWER: docs/db/tables-webhooks-search-and-infra.md",
